    "title": "Virginia DMV to Launch Agency's First Cannabis-Impaired Driving Prevention Campaign - NewsBreak",
    "text": "13 hours ago The Virginia Department of Motor Vehicles (DMV) has launched its first-ever cannabis-impaired driving campaign, encouraging Virginians to make the safe choice: if you get high to relax, then rela . Don’t drive high. Through a lighthearted and relatable message, the campaign reminds drivers that cannabis impairment can affect their ability to drive safely and that the best place to unwind is at home, not behind the wheel. Read full article",
